From 5dc44566b10aedbdec5a858876afa1aef33c254c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:28:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: smbb: allow monitored-battery

The power-supply core reads constant battery characteristics when SMBB
registers its battery interface with the device firmware node. Permit the
standard monitored-battery reference and include the common supply schema.

This allows firmware to describe an identified removable pack without
fixing its characteristics into the board DTS. With a RAM-only firmware
handoff, the existing LG Fx0 kernel exposes the supplied design capacity
and charge voltage and retains all five stock OCV tables. No gauge state
of charge or thermal-policy acceptance is implied.

Modified binding documentation and targeted generated DTB validation pass.

This change was developed with an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5)
during LG Fx0 bring-up. The assistant found the problem, wrote the change
and this message, and ran the tests described above.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml           | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml
index cbac55d3cb92..ca4fb7fa0b0b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,pm8941-charger.yaml
@@ -9,6 +9,9 @@ title: Qualcomm Switch-Mode Battery Charger and Boost
 maintainers:
   - Sebastian Reichel <sre@kernel.org>
 
+allOf:
+  - $ref: power-supply.yaml#
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
@@ -18,6 +21,8 @@ properties:
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  monitored-battery: true
+
   interrupts:
     items:
       - description: charge done
-- 
